-The decoder maps the fused branch embedding to two-dimensional residual predictions through a deep sequence of four ResBlocks followed by a linear output head. This deep sequence is necessary to process the complex interactions captured within the unified representation. The ResBlock structure provides sufficient representational capacity to capture the nonlinear mapping from the fused embedding to the residual dwell-time estimates. Simultaneously, the skip connections prevent representational collapse and support gradient flow during the local fine-tuning phase. This gradient propagation ensures that the RSU shadow model converges rapidly without disrupting the active content delivery tasks: \begin{equation} \text{ResBlock}(\mathbf{x}) = \text{ReGLU}\!\left(W_2\, \text{LayerNorm}\!\left(\text{Dropout}\!\left(\text{ReGLU}(W_1\, \text{LayerNorm}(\mathbf{x}))\right)\right)\right) + \mathbf{x} \label{eq:resblock} \end{equation} where $W_1, W_2 \in \mathbb{R}^{2d \times d}$ expand the dimension for the ReGLU operation and the skip connection restores dimension $d$ after the gating halves the width. The neural network stream output is: \begin{equation} P_\text{NN} = W_\text{out}\, \text{ResBlock}_4\!\left(\cdots \text{ResBlock}_1\!\left(\text{LayerNorm}(W_p\, \text{Flatten}(\mathbf{H}))\right)\cdots\right) \label{eq:decoder} \end{equation} where $W_p \in \mathbb{R}^{d_\text{branch} \times 3d_\text{branch}}$ projects the flattened fusion output back to dimension $d_\text{branch}$, and $W_\text{out} \in \mathbb{R}^{2 \times d_\text{branch}}$ is the output head producing $P_\text{NN} \in \mathbb{R}^2$. The output values directly translate into the expected time intervals required by the V2I chunk scheduler. By directly regressing the target parameters, the decoder entirely bypasses the complex sampling operations found in generative sampling architectures. This structural simplification guarantees deterministic, low-latency execution at the network edge. Therefore, the RSU can instantly allocate bandwidth resources and schedule proactive data transfers before the requesting vehicle departs.
+where $\text{ML\_Pred}$ signifies the prior machine learning output and $\text{NN\_Pred}$ represents the deep neural network estimation.
+In this mathematical hybrid construct, the scaling coefficients $\alpha$ and $\beta$ serve as continuously learnable vector parameters autonomously optimized during progressive local backpropagation cycles at the individual network edges.
+By initializing the algorithmic configuration to rely heavily upon the decision tree prior, the system dynamically establishes a foundational stabilization anchor that aggressively prevents immediate model collapse.
+As the localized infrastructure continuously accumulates distinct intersection traffic patterns, this adaptive gating mechanism logically expands the respective neural parameters, fundamentally shielding the architecture against catastrophic forgetting during incremental online fine-tuning iterations.
